\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces After a market fall, momentum ends up betting against the stocks most likely to rebound. Why momentum's beta flips (illustrative values). After a rising market the winners it holds are the high-beta stocks, so its net beta is positive. After a falling market the losers it sells short are the high-beta stocks, so its net beta turns strongly negative, and a sharp market rebound produces a large loss.}}{76}{figure.caption.20}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:05-beta}{{4.2}{76}{After a market fall, momentum ends up betting against the stocks most likely to rebound. Why momentum's beta flips (illustrative values). After a rising market the winners it holds are the high-beta stocks, so its net beta is positive. After a falling market the losers it sells short are the high-beta stocks, so its net beta turns strongly negative, and a sharp market rebound produces a large loss}{figure.caption.20}{}}
